insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('terms-of-service', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Terms of Service', 'The rules that govern your use of The Art of Connect website, apps and services.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

These Terms of Service ("Terms") are an agreement between you and **The Art of Connect, LLC** ("The Art of Connect," "we," "us" or "our"), a limited liability company organized under the laws of **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: state of LLC formation / registered address]**. They govern your use of theartofconnect.com, our member and professional portals, and every related service (together, the "Services").

By creating an account, checking the box to accept these Terms, or using the Services, you agree to these Terms and to the policies they reference, including our [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy), [Membership Agreement](/legal/membership-agreement), [Subscription and Automatic Renewal Policy](/legal/subscription-auto-renewal), [Cancellation and Refund Policy](/legal/refund-policy) and [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards). If you do not agree, do not use the Services.

## 1. Who we are and what we offer
The Art of Connect is a private membership community for adults aged 40 and older. We offer three experiences under one account:

- **The Professional Society — In Business:** professional networking, business compatibility, mentorship and collaboration.
- **The Art of Becoming — In Life:** self-discovery, personal development, private journaling and access to independent counselors, coaches and mentors.
- **The Personal Society — In Love:** intentional matchmaking for singles and relationship tools for couples.

Features may be added, changed or retired over time. Some features are available only with certain memberships.

## 2. Eligibility
- Consumer memberships are available only to adults aged **40 or older**, or any higher minimum age we publish. You confirm your date of birth when you register.
- We may ask you to verify your identity and age through an approved third-party provider. We do not store copies of government identification documents ourselves.
- Professional provider accounts (counselors, coaches, mentors and similar professionals) have separate requirements described in the [Professional Provider Agreement](/legal/professional-agreement).
- You may hold only one personal account. You may not use the Services if we have previously removed you, or if you are legally prohibited from doing so.

## 3. Your account
- Give us accurate, current information and keep it up to date.
- Keep your password private and use two-step verification where we offer it. You are responsible for activity on your account.
- Your account is personal. Do not share it, sell it or let anyone else use it. In a Couples Membership, each partner has their own separate account and login.
- Tell us right away at info@theartofconnect.com if you believe your account has been accessed without your permission.

## 4. Memberships and payment
Paid memberships, billing, automatic renewal, upgrades, downgrades and cancellation are governed by the [Membership Agreement](/legal/membership-agreement), the [Subscription and Automatic Renewal Policy](/legal/subscription-auto-renewal) and the [Cancellation and Refund Policy](/legal/refund-policy). Prices are those shown at checkout. Payments are processed by Stripe; we do not store your full card number.

## 5. Community conduct
You agree to follow our [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards). In particular, you will not:

- create fake profiles, impersonate anyone or misrepresent your age, identity, relationship status or credentials;
- ask other members for money, gifts, investments or financial information;
- harass, threaten, stalk or discriminate against anyone, or send unwanted sexual content;
- share another member's private information, messages or images without their permission;
- use the Services for unlawful purposes, spam, or unsolicited commercial promotion;
- scrape, copy, reverse engineer, overload or interfere with the Services or their security.

We may review reports, remove content, limit features, suspend or close accounts that violate these Terms or that put other people at risk, as described in our [Member Safety and Reporting Policy](/legal/safety-policy).

## 6. No guarantees about people or outcomes
We work to create a safe, respectful community, but we cannot guarantee:

- romantic compatibility, a match, or a successful relationship;
- business opportunities, referrals, partnerships or income;
- personal growth or any particular result from content, assessments or professional sessions;
- the identity, background, intentions or conduct of any member or professional.

Identity verification and compatibility assessments have limits and do not replace your own judgment. Please read our [Dating and Matchmaking Disclaimer](/legal/matchmaking-disclaimer) and [Business Networking Disclaimer](/legal/business-networking-disclaimer).

## 7. Professionals and wellness content
Counselors, coaches and mentors on the platform are **independent professionals**, not employees or agents of The Art of Connect. Coaching, mentorship, educational content and personal-development tools are not therapy, medical care or clinical treatment. **The Services are not an emergency service.** If you are in danger or in crisis, call 911 or your local emergency number, or call or text 988 in the United States. See our [Counseling, Coaching and Wellness Disclaimer](/legal/counseling-disclaimer).

## 8. Your content
You keep ownership of what you post or write ("Your Content"), including profile details, messages and private journal entries. You give us a limited licence to store, display and process Your Content only as needed to operate and provide the Services to you and the people you choose to share it with. We do not sell your private journals, assessments or confidential communications, and we do not use them for advertising or to train artificial-intelligence models. You are responsible for having the right to post Your Content.

## 9. Our intellectual property
The Art of Connect name, logos, sub-brand names, design, text, assessments and software belong to us or our licensors and are protected by law. You may use them only to use the Services as intended. See our [Intellectual Property and Copyright Policy](/legal/intellectual-property).

## 10. Privacy and communications
How we collect, use and protect personal information is described in our [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy). By using the Services you agree to receive account, billing, security and service messages electronically, as described in our [Electronic Communications and Consent Agreement](/legal/electronic-communications). Marketing messages are optional and require your separate consent.

## 11. Suspension and termination
You may close your account at any time from your account settings or by contacting us. We may suspend or close an account if we reasonably believe it violates these Terms, creates risk for others, is involved in fraud or a payment dispute, or if we are required to by law. Where appropriate and safe to do so, we will tell you why and explain how to appeal. Sections that by their nature should survive termination (including payment obligations, intellectual property, disclaimers, limitation of liability and dispute terms) survive.

## 12. Disclaimers
To the extent permitted by law, the Services are provided "as is" and "as available." We do not promise that the Services will be uninterrupted or error-free. **Nothing in these Terms limits any rights you have under applicable law that cannot be waived.**

## 13. Limitation of liability
To the extent permitted by law, The Art of Connect will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for the conduct of any member or professional, whether online or offline. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: liability cap amount and consumer-law carve-outs by state]**

## 14. Indemnity
You agree to cover reasonable losses we incur because of your breach of these Terms or your misuse of the Services, to the extent permitted by law. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: enforceability of consumer indemnity]**

## 15. Disputes and governing law
Before starting any formal claim, please contact us at info@theartofconnect.com so we can try to resolve the issue informally. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: governing law, venue, arbitration/class waiver]**

## 16. Changes to these Terms
We may update these Terms. If a change is material, we will tell you in advance by email or in the Services, show the effective date, and where required ask you to accept the updated version before you continue. The version you accepted, and when, is kept in your account records.

## 17. General
If any part of these Terms is found unenforceable, the rest remains in effect. Our failure to enforce a provision is not a waiver. You may not transfer your account or these Terms; we may assign them in connection with a merger, acquisition or sale of assets, with notice to you.

## 18. Contact
The Art of Connect, LLC · **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: state of LLC formation / registered address]** · info@theartofconnect.com$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('privacy-policy', 'Privacy Policy', 'privacy', 'How The Art of Connect collects, uses, protects and shares personal information, and the choices members have.', 'privacy', '{registration,professional}', '{}', 20);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('privacy-policy', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Privacy Policy', 'How The Art of Connect collects, uses, protects and shares personal information, and the choices members have.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

This Privacy Policy explains how **The Art of Connect, LLC** ("The Art of Connect," "we," "us") handles personal information when you visit theartofconnect.com, create an account, or use our membership experiences: **The Professional Society — In Business**, **The Art of Becoming — In Life**, and **The Personal Society — In Love**. Our services are offered only to adults aged 40 and older.

We wrote this policy to describe what our platform actually does. If a practice is not yet decided, we say so rather than guess.

## 1. Who we are and how to contact us
The Art of Connect, LLC is the company responsible for your personal information. Questions, requests and concerns can be sent to **info@theartofconnect.com**.

**[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: registered business mailing address to publish here]**

## 2. Information we collect

### 2.1 Information you give us
- **Account details:** your first name or display name, email address and password. Passwords are handled by our authentication provider and stored only in hashed form; we never see your password.
- **Date of birth:** collected at registration to confirm you are 40 or older. It is stored in a private record that only you can read. Our staff, including the owner, see only whether your account meets the age requirement, never the date itself.
- **Membership choices:** the experiences, membership package, billing interval and any add-ons you select.
- **Profile and experience content:** information you choose to add within each experience, such as professional interests in In Business or relationship preferences in In Love.
- **Private journals and assessments:** reflections, journal entries and assessment answers you create, particularly in In Life and In Love.
- **Communications:** messages you exchange with other members or professionals through the platform, and messages you send to us.
- **Professional applications:** for counselors, coaches and mentors, your legal name, professional type, license or credential details, specialties and related information you submit for verification.
- **Reports and safety information:** reports you file about another member, and blocks you place.

### 2.2 Information collected automatically
- **Security information:** when you sign in, reset a password or submit protected forms, we record the event type, time and a **one-way hash** of your IP address together with a shortened browser description. We do not store raw IP addresses in these logs, and logs never contain passwords, journal entries or message contents.
- **Essential cookies:** used to keep you signed in and secure. See our [Cookie and Tracking Policy](/legal/cookie-policy).
- **Campaign attribution:** if you arrive from a marketing link or a member's referral link, we store the campaign source and referral code in a first-party cookie so we can credit the referral.

### 2.3 Information from service providers
- **Payments:** Stripe tells us whether a payment succeeded, failed or was refunded, along with amounts and dates. We never receive or store your full card number.
- **Identity verification:** if identity verification is required, Stripe Identity tells us the outcome (for example, verified or not verified). We do not receive or store images of your government ID or your selfie.
- **Bot protection:** Cloudflare Turnstile tells us whether a form submission passed a bot check.

## 3. Sensitive information
Some information you share is especially personal: private journals, personal and relationship assessments, romantic preferences, private communications, identity verification results, financial and billing information, professional credentials, and account security information. We protect it as follows:
- **Private journals, assessments and confidential communications are not visible to our staff, including the owner.** Our database rules restrict them to you (and, for communications, the other participants).
- We **do not sell** sensitive personal information.
- We **do not use** private journals, assessments or confidential communications **for advertising or to train artificial intelligence models.**
- We **never include** journal entries, assessment answers, dates of birth or message contents **in emails**.

**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: CCPA/CPRA "sensitive personal information" notices and the right to limit use]**
**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: state consumer health data laws (e.g. Washington My Health My Data, Nevada, Connecticut) as they may apply to In Life journals and assessments]**
**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: whether HIPAA applies — we do not currently claim HIPAA compliance and do not provide clinical treatment]**

## 4. How we use information
We use personal information to:
1. Create and secure your account, including verifying that you are 40 or older.
2. Provide the experiences you choose and the features within them.
3. Process membership payments, renewals, upgrades, cancellations and refunds through Stripe.
4. Send transactional emails, such as account, membership, payment and safety notices.
5. Keep the community safe: detect fake profiles, investigate reports, prevent fraud and enforce our [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards).
6. Verify professional credentials before a professional is listed.
7. Protect our systems, including bot protection and security monitoring.
8. Comply with law and respond to lawful requests.
9. Understand, in aggregate, how memberships are used so we can improve the service.

We send marketing emails only where you have opted in, and marketing consent is always separate from accepting our agreements. You can withdraw marketing consent at any time.

## 5. Keeping your experiences separate
In Business, In Life and In Love are kept separate. Information you create in one experience is not shared with members of another experience unless you choose to share it.

**Couples** each have their own individual account, password and private space. Your partner cannot read your private journal or individual assessments. You decide what, if anything, is shared in your shared relationship space, and you can change that choice.

## 6. How we share information
We share personal information only as described here:
- **With other members, as you direct:** for example, profile details you choose to show to potential matches or professional connections.
- **With professionals you choose to work with:** only the information you choose to share with them.
- **With our service providers**, who process information on our behalf under contract:
  - **Supabase** — database and authentication hosting.
  - **Netlify** — website hosting and delivery.
  - **Stripe** — payment processing and, where used, **Stripe Identity** for identity and age verification.
  - **Resend** — delivery of transactional email.
  - **Cloudflare** — Turnstile bot protection on our forms.
  - **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: any additional providers, e.g. analytics, error monitoring, scheduling or video services, must be added here before use]**
- **For legal reasons:** to comply with law, legal process or lawful government requests, to protect the safety of any person, or to investigate fraud or security issues. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: process and standards for responding to law-enforcement requests]**
- **In a business transaction:** if The Art of Connect is involved in a merger, acquisition, financing or sale of assets, personal information may be transferred as part of that transaction, subject to this policy and applicable law. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: notice requirements for business transfers]**

We do not sell personal information and do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: confirm "sale"/"share" definitions under applicable state laws]**

## 7. Who at The Art of Connect can see your information
Staff access is limited by role (for example, support, moderation, finance), and every staff account must use two-factor authentication. Staff actions on sensitive records are recorded in audit logs. Owner access does not include private journals, assessments or confidential communications.

## 8. How we protect information
- Database row-level security so members can read only their own private records.
- Encryption in transit (HTTPS) across our website and service providers.
- Mandatory two-factor authentication for staff.
- Bot protection and rate limiting on sign-in, registration, password recovery and other public forms.
- Security logs that use hashed IP addresses and exclude passwords and private content.

No system is perfectly secure. If we learn of a security incident affecting your personal information, we will notify you and regulators as required by law. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: state breach-notification timelines and content requirements]**

## 9. Retention and deletion
We keep personal information only as long as needed for the purposes described here, to meet legal obligations, and to resolve disputes. Details are in our [Data Retention and Account Deletion Policy](/legal/data-retention).

**[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: retention period for closed accounts]**

## 10. Your choices and rights
You can:
- Access and update your account information in your account settings.
- Request a copy of your personal information.
- Request deletion of your account and personal information, subject to legal retention requirements.
- Withdraw optional consents (such as marketing) at any time.
- Control what you share with matches, professionals and, for couples, your partner.

Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights, including rights to correct, delete, or obtain a portable copy of your information, to limit use of sensitive information, and to appeal our decision on a request. Send requests to **info@theartofconnect.com**. We will verify your identity before acting on a request and will not discriminate against you for exercising your rights.

**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: state-by-state privacy rights (California, Colorado, Connecticut, Virginia, Texas, Oregon and others), response timelines and appeal process]**

## 11. Age requirement
Our services are only for adults aged 40 and older. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone younger than the minimum age, and we do not direct our services to children. If we learn that an account belongs to someone under the minimum age, we will close it.

## 12. International users
Our services are operated in the United States and intended for users in the United States. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether to accept members outside the United States]** **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: cross-border transfer requirements if non-US members are accepted]**

## 13. Changes to this policy
If we make material changes, we will notify you by email or in your account before they take effect and, where required, ask for your consent again. The effective date and version appear at the top of this policy.

## 14. Contact
The Art of Connect, LLC — **info@theartofconnect.com**$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

