insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('membership-agreement', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Membership Agreement', 'What your paid membership includes, how billing works, and how to change or cancel it.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

This Membership Agreement ("Agreement") applies when you purchase a paid membership from **The Art of Connect, LLC** ("we," "us"). It forms part of our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service) and works together with our [Subscription and Automatic Renewal Policy](/legal/subscription-auto-renewal) and [Cancellation and Refund Policy](/legal/refund-policy).

## 1. Membership eligibility
- You must be **40 or older** (or meet any higher minimum age we publish) and hold an account in good standing.
- We may require identity and age verification through an approved third-party provider before some features are available, for example matchmaking introductions.
- Memberships are for personal use by the account holder only.

## 2. Membership options
The memberships available, their names, what each includes and their prices are shown on our Memberships page and at checkout. They currently fall into these groups:

- **Individual experiences:** The Professional Society (In Business), The Art of Becoming (In Life) and The Personal Society (In Love, for singles).
- **Couples Membership (In Love):** for two partners. Each partner has a **separate individual account**, gives their own consent, and controls what personal information is shared with the other. See the [Couples Membership Agreement](/legal/couples-agreement).
- **Bundles:** two experiences together (for example Dual Society — In Business and In Love; Business + Life; Life + Love) or all three (Complete Society), at a bundled rate.
- **Exclusive memberships:** Executive Private and Elite Concierge, which include all three experiences and additional benefits described at checkout. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: final concierge benefits and their limits before Elite Concierge is sold]**

Professional provider subscriptions are governed by the [Professional Provider Agreement](/legal/professional-agreement), not this Agreement.

## 3. One account, every device
Your membership is one account that you can use on your phone, tablet and computer. **There are no additional device charges.** Sharing your login with another person is not permitted.

## 4. Price and what you pay
- You pay the price shown at checkout for the membership and billing period you choose, plus any applicable taxes. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: sales tax / digital services tax obligations by state]**
- An **onboarding fee** applies only if it is clearly shown at checkout before you pay. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether any onboarding fee applies, and to which memberships]**
- Annual memberships may be offered at a reduced price compared with paying monthly. The annual price is shown at checkout.
- Payments are processed securely by Stripe. We never see or store your full card number.

## 5. Billing periods and automatic renewal
Memberships are billed **monthly or annually**, as you choose, and **renew automatically** at the end of each period until you cancel. Before you pay, checkout shows the price, the billing frequency, when you will next be charged and how to cancel, and asks for your affirmative consent. Full details are in the [Subscription and Automatic Renewal Policy](/legal/subscription-auto-renewal).

## 6. Promotional codes and offers
- Promotional codes apply only as described with the offer. Unless the offer says otherwise, a code applies to your **first billing period only**, after which the regular price applies.
- Codes may have expiry dates, usage limits or apply only to certain memberships. They have no cash value and cannot be combined unless stated.
- We may withdraw a code that was issued in error or used in violation of its terms.

## 7. Upgrades and downgrades
- You can change your membership (for example, add an experience, move to a bundle, or switch between monthly and annual billing) from **My membership**.
- Changes take effect immediately. Our payment processor calculates a **prorated** charge or credit for the rest of the current billing period, which appears on your next invoice.
- When you remove an experience, your access to it ends when the change takes effect. Your private journal and other personal records are kept in your account unless you delete them, as described in our [Data Retention and Account Deletion Policy](/legal/data-retention).

## 8. Failed payments
If a renewal payment fails, our payment processor will try again over a short period and we will notify you by email so you can update your payment method. If payment still cannot be collected, we may **suspend paid features** until the balance is paid, or end the membership. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: length of grace period before suspension]**

## 9. Cancellation
You can cancel online at any time from **My membership**, without calling or emailing us. Cancellation stops future renewals. Your access continues until the end of the period you have already paid for. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: any cancellation fee — none assumed]** Refunds are covered by the [Cancellation and Refund Policy](/legal/refund-policy).

## 10. Price changes
We may change membership prices in the future. We will give you advance notice by email before a new price applies to your renewal, and you can cancel before it takes effect. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: advance notice period for price changes — at least 30 days recommended for attorney review]**

## 11. Chargebacks and payment disputes
If you believe you were charged in error, please contact us first at info@theartofconnect.com; most issues can be resolved quickly. If you file a chargeback with your bank, we may **suspend your account while the dispute is open** and provide your transaction records to the payment processor. Filing a chargeback does not remove your right to dispute a charge under applicable law.

## 12. Membership features and safety
Membership gives access to features; it does not guarantee introductions, matches, business opportunities or results. We may change features over time and will tell you about material reductions in what your membership includes. We may suspend or end a membership for violations of our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service) or [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards) under our [Member Safety and Reporting Policy](/legal/safety-policy). **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether any refund applies when a membership is ended for a violation]**

## 13. Your statutory rights
**Nothing in this Agreement limits rights you have under applicable law**, including any cooling-off, cancellation or refund rights provided by state dating-service or consumer-protection laws. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: state dating-service contract laws (cancellation windows, required notices) for In Love memberships]**

## 14. Contact
Questions about your membership: info@theartofconnect.com$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('subscription-auto-renewal', 'Subscription and Automatic Renewal Policy', 'membership', 'How recurring billing works, what we tell you before you subscribe, and how to stop renewal online.', 'auto_renewal', '{checkout,professional}', '{}', 60);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('subscription-auto-renewal', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Subscription and Automatic Renewal Policy', 'How recurring billing works, what we tell you before you subscribe, and how to stop renewal online.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

This policy explains how recurring memberships and professional provider subscriptions with **The Art of Connect, LLC** renew, what we disclose before you subscribe, and how to stop renewal. It forms part of our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service) and [Membership Agreement](/legal/membership-agreement). **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: state automatic-renewal law requirements, e.g. California, New York]**

## 1. Which plans renew automatically
- All paid member memberships (individual, Couples, bundles, Complete Society, Executive Private and Elite Concierge).
- All professional provider subscriptions (Standard, Professional and Premium Provider).

Each plan is billed either **monthly** or **annually**, as you select at checkout.

## 2. What we show you before you subscribe
Before you are charged, checkout clearly displays, close to the payment button:

- the membership name and what it includes;
- the recurring price and billing frequency (per month or per year), plus any taxes;
- any one-time onboarding fee, if one applies;
- any promotional price, how long it lasts, and the regular price that follows;
- that the subscription **continues until you cancel**;
- the date of your first renewal charge;
- how to cancel online.

## 3. Your affirmative consent
We will not start a recurring subscription unless you **actively agree** to the automatic renewal terms, for example by ticking a box that is **not pre-selected** and confirming your purchase. We keep a record of your consent, including the version of this policy, the date and time, and the plan you selected.

## 4. Confirmation after purchase
After you subscribe we send an email confirmation that includes the automatic renewal terms, the price and billing frequency, the cancellation method, and information on how to contact us. You can also view these details at any time under **My membership**.

## 5. When and how you are charged
- **Monthly plans** renew on the same day each month as your start date (or the closest valid date).
- **Annual plans** renew once a year on your start anniversary.
- Charges are made to the payment method on file through our payment processor, Stripe. You can update your payment method under **My membership**.

## 6. Reminders before renewal
- **Annual plans:** we send a reminder email before each annual renewal with the renewal date, price and how to cancel. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: reminder timing — 15 to 45 days before annual renewal suggested; ATTORNEY REVIEW: state-specific notice windows]**
- **Free trials or promotional periods**, if offered: we tell you before the regular price begins. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether free trials will be offered]**

## 7. Price changes
If the price of your plan changes, we will email you before the new price applies to your next renewal and give you the chance to cancel first. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: advance notice period for price changes — at least 30 days recommended for attorney review]**

## 8. How to stop automatic renewal
- Go to **My membership** and select **Cancel membership**. You can do this online at any time, in a few steps, without contacting us.
- Cancellation takes effect at the **end of your current billing period**; you keep access until then and are not charged again.
- We send an email confirming your cancellation.
- You can also email info@theartofconnect.com and we will process your request.

**[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: any cancellation fee — none assumed]**

## 9. Failed renewals
If a renewal payment fails, the processor retries the charge and we email you. Paid features may be suspended if payment cannot be collected after the retry period. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: length of grace period before suspension]**

## 10. Refunds
Renewal charges are handled under our [Cancellation and Refund Policy](/legal/refund-policy).

## 11. Changing plans or billing frequency
- You can switch between monthly and annual billing, add or remove experiences, or move between individual, bundled and exclusive memberships from **My membership**.
- When you change plans, the new plan continues to renew automatically on its own billing cycle. Checkout shows the new recurring price and renewal date before you confirm.
- The difference in price for the current period is **prorated** by our payment processor and appears on your next invoice.

## 12. Bundles, couples and exclusive memberships
- A bundle (for example Dual Society or Complete Society) is **one subscription** with one renewal date, not separate subscriptions for each experience.
- In a **Couples Membership**, each partner keeps a separate individual account. The renewal terms, price and cancellation method are shown to the partner who purchases the membership. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: which partner is billed and whether both partners must consent to renewal]**
- Executive Private and Elite Concierge renew on the same terms as other memberships unless different terms are shown at checkout.

## 13. Professional provider subscriptions
Standard, Professional and Premium Provider subscriptions renew automatically on the same basis. Providers receive the same disclosures, confirmations, reminders and online cancellation option described in this policy. A provider's subscription is separate from any fees their clients pay for sessions.

## 14. Records we keep
For each subscription we keep a record of the plan, price, billing frequency, the disclosures shown, your consent (version, date and time), confirmation and reminder emails sent, and any cancellation. These records help resolve questions about charges and are kept under our [Data Retention and Account Deletion Policy](/legal/data-retention).

## 15. Your rights
**Nothing in this policy limits rights you have under applicable law**, including any right to cancel or receive a refund provided by state automatic-renewal, dating-service or consumer-protection laws.

## 16. Contact
info@theartofconnect.com$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

