insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('couples-agreement', 'Couples Membership Agreement', 'membership', 'How couples memberships work, including separate accounts, independent consent, private information and what happens if a couple separates.', 'couples', '{couples}', '{personal-society}', 80);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('couples-agreement', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Couples Membership Agreement', 'How couples memberships work, including separate accounts, independent consent, private information and what happens if a couple separates.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

This Couples Membership Agreement ("Agreement") applies when two people use a couples membership offered by The Art of Connect, LLC ("The Art of Connect," "we," "us"), including the Couples Membership in **The Personal Society** (In Love) and any couples option added to a bundled membership. It supplements our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service), [Membership Agreement](/legal/membership-agreement), [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy) and [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards). Each partner must accept this Agreement individually.

## 1. Who may join
- Both partners must be adults aged 40 or older (or any higher minimum age we set) and must meet all other eligibility requirements.
- Both partners must be in a committed relationship with each other and must each **freely and independently choose** to participate. No one may be enrolled in a couples membership without their own consent.
- We may ask either partner to complete identity and age verification.

## 2. Two separate individual accounts
- **Each partner has their own account, email address and password.** Accounts may not be shared, and one partner may not log in as the other.
- Each partner accepts our terms and privacy choices for themselves, and each controls their own notification, privacy and marketing preferences.
- Each partner may report or block any member, and may contact us privately, without the other partner's knowledge.

## 3. Your private information stays yours
- **Nothing is shared automatically.** Your private journal entries, personal reflections, individual assessment answers and messages with professionals remain private to you unless you choose to share them.
- The couples experience provides a **shared space** for content that both partners deliberately add. You decide, item by item, what to place there.
- You may stop sharing at any time. Content you have already shared may remain visible to your partner where it has been copied into the shared space; you may remove items you contributed. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether removing shared content removes it from the partner's view immediately, and whether shared-space history is retained.]**
- Our staff do not disclose one partner's private information to the other partner, and couples features are never used to monitor a partner.
- Your private information is never sold, used for advertising or used for artificial intelligence training, as described in our [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy).

## 4. Independent consent
- Consent to connect as a couple must be given separately by each partner, through their own account.
- Either partner may withdraw consent and disconnect the couple link at any time, without the other partner's agreement.
- If you feel pressured to participate or to share information, please contact us at info@theartofconnect.com. You may also disconnect privately.

## 5. Billing and responsibility for payment
- A couples membership is purchased by one partner (the **"purchasing account"**). The purchasing account holder is responsible for all charges, renewals, upgrades and cancellations, under our [Membership Agreement](/legal/membership-agreement), [Subscription and Automatic Renewal Policy](/legal/subscription-auto-renewal) and [Cancellation and Refund Policy](/legal/refund-policy).
- The other partner's access to couples features depends on the purchasing account's membership remaining active.
- Billing information belongs to the purchasing account and is not visible to the other partner.
- **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether partners may split payment or transfer the purchasing role.]**

## 6. Couples tools are not counseling
Guided conversations, exercises and relationship content are educational and personal-development resources, not couples therapy, marriage counseling or clinical treatment. If you choose to work with a licensed professional through the platform, that relationship is governed by our [Counseling, Coaching and Wellness Disclaimer](/legal/counseling-disclaimer) and the provider's own terms. **The Art of Connect cannot guarantee the success of any relationship.**

## 7. Safety within the relationship
If you are experiencing abuse, coercion or threats from your partner:
- you may disconnect the couple link and change your password at any time;
- you may contact us privately at info@theartofconnect.com, and we will not inform your partner that you contacted us;
- in an emergency, call **911**; the National Domestic Violence Hotline is available at 1-800-799-7233; for emotional crisis, call or text **988**.

The Art of Connect is not an emergency service.

## 8. If you separate or one partner leaves
- Either partner may leave the couples membership at any time by disconnecting the couple link.
- After disconnection, each partner keeps their own individual account and private content. Neither partner receives access to the other's private content.
- **Shared-space content:** **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: what happens to shared-space content after separation — e.g. each partner keeps a copy of what they contributed, or the shared space is closed for both.]**
- **Membership and billing:** the purchasing account remains responsible for the membership until it is changed or cancelled. The purchasing partner may downgrade to an individual membership or cancel. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether the non-purchasing partner is offered a transition to their own membership, and on what terms.]**
- A former partner may not use The Personal Society singles features while still holding an active couples link. After separation, a member may choose a singles membership like any other member.

## 9. Ending the couples membership
Cancellation of the couples membership by the purchasing account ends couples features for both partners at the end of the current billing period, subject to our [Cancellation and Refund Policy](/legal/refund-policy). Each partner's individual account, private content and data rights continue under our [Data Retention and Account Deletion Policy](/legal/data-retention). Either partner may delete their own account; doing so does not delete the other partner's account.

## 10. Conduct
Both partners must follow our [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards). If one partner's account is suspended or closed for a violation, we will take reasonable steps to preserve the other partner's individual account and privacy.

## 11. Changes
We may update this Agreement. Where changes are material, we will notify both partners and, where required, ask each to accept the updated version individually. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: notice and renewed-acceptance requirements.]**

## 12. Legal review items
**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: obligations to a non-paying partner under consumer and auto-renewal laws; privacy rights of each partner over shared content; interaction with state dating-service statutes.]**

## 13. Contact
**info@theartofconnect.com**$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('business-networking-disclaimer', 'Business Networking Disclaimer', 'disclaimer', 'The Professional Society connects members for professional networking and mentorship; it does not provide investment, legal, financial or employment advice.', 'business_networking', '{checkout}', '{professional-society}', 90);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('business-networking-disclaimer', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Business Networking Disclaimer', 'The Professional Society connects members for professional networking and mentorship; it does not provide investment, legal, financial or employment advice.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

This disclaimer applies to **The Professional Society** (In Business) and to any business introductions, mentorship, networking, collaboration tools, events or professional content offered by The Art of Connect, LLC ("The Art of Connect," "we," "us"). It forms part of our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service) and [Membership Agreement](/legal/membership-agreement).

## 1. What The Professional Society is
The Professional Society is a private networking community for accomplished adults aged 40 and older. It helps members discover people with complementary experience, exchange ideas, find mentors and explore possible collaborations. It is a place to meet people — not a source of professional advice, a marketplace for securities or an employment agency.

## 2. No investment, legal, financial, tax or employment advice
- Nothing provided through The Professional Society — including introductions, compatibility insights, content, events, member conversations or mentor discussions — is **investment, securities, legal, accounting, tax, financial, insurance or employment advice.**
- Information shared by members and mentors reflects their own views and experience. They are not acting on behalf of The Art of Connect.
- Before making any business, investment, legal, financial or career decision, consult a qualified, licensed professional who can consider your circumstances.

## 3. Not a securities or investment platform
- The Art of Connect is **not a broker-dealer, investment adviser, funding portal, crowdfunding platform or exchange,** and does not facilitate, recommend or participate in the offer or sale of securities or investments.
- **Members may not use The Professional Society to solicit investments,** offer securities, raise capital from members or promote trading, cryptocurrency or "guaranteed return" schemes. Such conduct violates our [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards) and may be unlawful.
- If someone pitches you an investment through the platform, decline, stop contact and report it.

**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: securities-law considerations for any future features involving capital raising, accredited-investor networking or investor introductions; confirm current prohibitions are sufficient.]**

## 4. Do your own due diligence
- **We do not vet business proposals, companies, financial claims, credentials or track records** of members, except where we expressly state that a specific credential has been verified for a professional provider.
- You are solely responsible for evaluating any person, company or opportunity, including checking references, licenses, financial statements and legal standing, and for any agreement you enter into with another member.
- Put important agreements in writing and seek independent professional advice.

## 5. No endorsement
An introduction, a "verified" badge, a featured profile, membership level or appearance at an event is **not an endorsement** by The Art of Connect of any member, business, product, service or opportunity. Identity verification confirms only that a document appeared to match the person at a point in time; it says nothing about their business or financial standing.

## 6. No guarantee of opportunities
**The Art of Connect cannot guarantee business opportunities,** clients, partnerships, investments, employment, revenue or any other professional outcome, or the conduct of any member. Your membership provides access to the community and its tools during your membership.

## 7. Employment and hiring
The Professional Society is not an employment agency or recruiting service. If you use a connection to hire or be hired, you are responsible for complying with employment, anti-discrimination, contractor-classification and privacy laws. Do not use member information for unsolicited recruiting or mass outreach.

## 8. Confidential business information
- Share confidential or proprietary information only with people you trust, and consider a written non-disclosure agreement.
- Do not share another member's confidential business information without their permission.
- The Art of Connect is not responsible for the misuse of information you choose to share with other members.

## 9. Mentors and professional providers
Mentors and coaches who offer services through the platform are independent. Their services are governed by our [Professional Provider Agreement](/legal/professional-agreement) and [Counseling, Coaching and Wellness Disclaimer](/legal/counseling-disclaimer), and by any separate agreement you make with them. Mentorship is not licensed professional advice unless the provider is licensed and expressly provides a licensed service within their scope.

## 10. Intellectual property and collaboration
- Ideas, business plans, designs and other materials you share remain yours, but sharing them does not by itself create any legal protection or obligation of confidentiality on the part of other members.
- If you collaborate with another member, agree in writing who owns the work, how revenue or equity is shared, and how either of you can end the collaboration.
- The Art of Connect does not take any ownership interest in, or responsibility for, ventures formed between members, and is not a party to agreements between members.
- Do not post or share another person's copyrighted material, trademarks or trade secrets without permission; see our [Intellectual Property and Copyright Policy](/legal/intellectual-property).

## 11. Conduct and reporting
Business conversations must remain professional and respectful. Unwanted romantic or sexual approaches have no place in The Professional Society. Report spam, fraud, harassment or unwanted solicitation through the member area or at info@theartofconnect.com, as described in our [Member Safety and Reporting Policy](/legal/safety-policy).

## 12. Limitation of liability
To the fullest extent permitted by law, The Art of Connect is not liable for any business, investment, financial or employment loss arising from your interactions or dealings with other members or third parties. Nothing here limits rights that cannot be waived under applicable law. See our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service) for full terms. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: enforceability of this limitation and any required consumer-law carve-outs.]**

## 13. Emergencies
The Art of Connect is not an emergency service. In an emergency, call **911**.

## 14. Contact
Questions about The Professional Society: **info@theartofconnect.com**.$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('counseling-disclaimer', 'Counseling, Coaching and Wellness Disclaimer', 'disclaimer', 'What the personal-growth tools, coaching, mentorship and professional services on The Art of Connect are, and what they are not.', 'wellness_disclaimer', '{checkout,professional}', '{art-of-becoming}', 100);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('counseling-disclaimer', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Counseling, Coaching and Wellness Disclaimer', 'What the personal-growth tools, coaching, mentorship and professional services on The Art of Connect are, and what they are not.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

This disclaimer explains the nature of the personal-growth and professional services available through **The Art of Connect, LLC** ("The Art of Connect," "we," "us"), especially in **The Art of Becoming — In Life**. It applies to every member and is part of our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service).

## 1. Not an emergency service

The Art of Connect is **not an emergency service**. We do not monitor journals, messages, assessments or appointments in real time.

**If you are in crisis or may harm yourself or someone else, call 911 (or your local emergency number) right away. In the United States you can also call or text 988 to reach the 988 Suicide & Crisis Lifeline.**

## 2. The Art of Connect does not provide clinical treatment

The Art of Connect is a membership platform for adults aged **40 and older**. The company itself does **not diagnose, treat or provide clinical care** for any mental-health or medical condition. Nothing on the platform replaces care from a qualified licensed professional.

## 3. Different kinds of support, clearly distinguished

You may encounter four different kinds of support on the platform. They are not the same:

- **Personal development and educational content.** The Art of Becoming offers guided reflection, a private journal, emotional-intelligence exercises and educational content. These are self-reflection tools for personal growth.
- **Coaching.** Coaches help you set and pursue goals in areas such as relationships, career or wellbeing. **Coaching is not therapy.** Coaches do not diagnose or treat mental-health conditions.
- **Mentorship.** Mentors in The Professional Society share their professional experience. Mentorship is not legal, financial, tax or investment advice unless a mentor holds the relevant license and clearly says they are acting in that capacity.
- **Licensed mental-health services.** Licensed professionals, such as licensed counselors, therapists, social workers or psychologists, may offer services only where they are licensed to practice and only within the scope of their license. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: whether licensed clinical services and telehealth sessions will be offered through the platform at launch.]**

Each professional's profile states the category they were approved under. Please read it before booking.

## 4. Assessments and journals are for self-reflection

Compatibility, readiness, personality and emotional-intelligence assessments, and the private journal, are **self-reflection tools**. They:

- are **not** psychological tests or clinical evaluations;
- do **not** diagnose any condition;
- do **not** predict the success of a relationship, partnership or business venture.

Your private journal entries and assessment answers stay private to you. They are never shared with other members, professionals or our staff unless you choose to share them, and they are never used for advertising or to train artificial-intelligence models. See our [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy).

## 5. Professionals are independent

Counselors, coaches and mentors on the platform are **independent professionals**, not employees or agents of The Art of Connect. They are responsible for their own services, advice, records and professional conduct.

When a professional shows a **verified** badge, our staff completed identity and credential checks, such as a license lookup and disciplinary-record review, at the time of verification. Verification:

- is a point-in-time check of the information available to us;
- does **not** guarantee a professional's skill, judgment, conduct or results;
- does **not** mean The Art of Connect supervises or endorses their services.

You remain responsible for choosing a professional who suits your needs. Licensing boards in your state can confirm a license's current status.

## 6. No guaranteed outcomes

Personal growth is personal. The Art of Connect, its content and the professionals on it **cannot guarantee** any outcome, including emotional wellbeing, relationship success, reconciliation, marriage, career or business results.

## 7. Consult qualified professionals

Talk to a qualified professional before making significant decisions about your health, wellbeing, relationships, finances or legal matters. If you have a medical or mental-health condition, consult your physician or a licensed mental-health professional. Do not stop or change any treatment based on content from the platform.

## 8. Privacy of what you share with professionals

What you choose to share with a professional is governed by our [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy) and by that professional's own obligations. The Art of Connect is **not represented as HIPAA compliant**, and platform messaging should not be relied on as a clinical record. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: HIPAA applicability and health-information privacy obligations before any clinical services are enabled.]**

## 9. Reporting concerns

If a professional behaves inappropriately, misrepresents their credentials or makes you feel unsafe, report it through the platform's reporting tools or by email to **info@theartofconnect.com**. See our [Member Safety and Reporting Policy](/legal/safety-policy).

## 10. Contact

The Art of Connect, LLC · **info@theartofconnect.com**$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('matchmaking-disclaimer', 'Dating and Matchmaking Disclaimer', 'disclaimer', 'What The Personal Society''s introductions and compatibility tools can and cannot do.', 'matchmaking', '{checkout}', '{personal-society}', 110);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('matchmaking-disclaimer', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Dating and Matchmaking Disclaimer', 'What The Personal Society''s introductions and compatibility tools can and cannot do.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

This disclaimer applies to **The Personal Society** (In Love), including singles memberships, couples memberships, compatibility assessments, introductions, concierge or personalized introductions, events and any related features offered by The Art of Connect, LLC ("The Art of Connect," "we," "us"). It forms part of our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service) and [Membership Agreement](/legal/membership-agreement). Please read it carefully before using these services.

## 1. Our purpose
The Personal Society is designed for adults aged 40 and older who want to approach relationships with intention. We offer tools that encourage self-reflection, thoughtful introductions and respectful connection. We are a membership community, not a guarantee of any relationship.

## 2. No guarantee of compatibility or outcome
**The Art of Connect cannot guarantee romantic compatibility, a successful relationship, marriage, a particular number of introductions, a response from any member, or any other outcome.** Attraction and lasting relationships depend on the choices and circumstances of the people involved, which are beyond our control. Your membership fee pays for access to the platform and its features during your membership — not for a result.

**[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether any membership (e.g. Elite Concierge) promises a minimum number of personalized introductions or a specific service level. If so, it must be stated precisely in the Membership Agreement.]**

## 3. Compatibility assessments and insights
- Assessments, readiness reflections and compatibility insights are tools for reflection and conversation. They are **not** psychological evaluations, clinical diagnoses or scientific predictions of relationship success.
- Results depend on the honesty and completeness of the answers given by each person, which we cannot verify.
- Your individual assessment answers are private. We may use them to suggest introductions as described in our [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy), but we do not show your answers to other members, sell them, or use them for advertising or artificial intelligence training.

## 4. Introductions and personalized matchmaking
- Introductions are suggestions. You are always free to decline, and others are free to decline you.
- Where introductions are made by a person (for example, a concierge), they reflect that person's judgment based on the information available. They are not a professional recommendation or an endorsement of the other member.
- We do not conduct in-depth investigations into members' backgrounds, finances, health or relationship histories.

## 5. We do not screen for everything
- **Identity and age verification**, where completed, confirms only that a document appeared to match the person at the time of the check. It is not a background check and does not confirm someone's marital status, intentions, character or conduct. See our [Identity and Age Verification Policy](/legal/identity-verification).
- **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether background checks are offered.]** Unless and until we state otherwise in writing, **The Art of Connect does not conduct criminal background checks or sex-offender registry screening of members.**
- We rely on members to provide truthful information and on our community to report concerns.

## 6. Responsibility for your own interactions
**The Art of Connect cannot guarantee another person's conduct.** You are responsible for your own decisions about whom you communicate with and meet, what you share and how you protect yourself. Please follow the safe meeting guidance in our [Member Safety and Reporting Policy](/legal/safety-policy), including:
- video calling before meeting;
- meeting in a public place;
- telling a friend where you will be;
- using your own transportation;
- never sending money or sharing financial information.

## 7. Romance scams
Anyone who asks you for money, gift cards, cryptocurrency, loans or investments — however genuine their story appears — should be treated as a likely scam. Stop contact and report them. We will never ask you to send money to another member.

## 8. Relationship status and honesty
Singles memberships are intended for people who are unattached and open to a relationship. Members must be truthful about their relationship status. Couples memberships are for people already in a relationship and are governed by our [Couples Membership Agreement](/legal/couples-agreement). Misrepresenting your status is a violation of our [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards).

## 9. Not counseling or therapy
Relationship content, guided conversations and couples tools are educational and personal-development resources. They are not marriage counseling, therapy or clinical treatment. Licensed professional services, if offered through the platform, are provided by independent providers under separate terms — see our [Counseling, Coaching and Wellness Disclaimer](/legal/counseling-disclaimer).

## 10. Events
If we host or promote events, attendance is voluntary and at your own risk. Other attendees are not screened beyond any verification stated for that event. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: event liability waivers and venue requirements.]**

## 11. Limitation of liability
To the fullest extent permitted by law, The Art of Connect is not responsible for the conduct of any member or third party, online or offline, or for any loss arising from your interactions with others. Nothing in this disclaimer limits rights you have under law that cannot be waived, or our responsibility for our own negligence or misconduct where the law does not allow that responsibility to be limited. The full terms are in our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service). **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: enforceability of limitation-of-liability language for dating services in each state where we operate.]**

## 12. State dating-service laws
Some states regulate online dating and matchmaking services, including required safety awareness notices, background-check disclosures, contract cancellation rights and limits on contract length or price. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: state dating-service laws (e.g. safety awareness notices, background-check disclosures in states such as New York, New Jersey, Illinois, Texas, Florida), dating-service contract statutes (e.g. three-day cancellation rights, maximum terms) and any required disclosures at sign-up.]**

## 13. Emergencies
The Art of Connect is not an emergency service. If you are in danger, call **911**. For emotional crisis, call or text **988**.

## 14. Contact
Questions about The Personal Society: **info@theartofconnect.com**.$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('professional-agreement', 'Professional Provider Agreement', 'professional', 'The terms that apply to counselors, coaches, mentors and other professionals who offer services through The Art of Connect.', 'professional_agreement', '{professional}', '{}', 120);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('professional-agreement', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Professional Provider Agreement', 'The terms that apply to counselors, coaches, mentors and other professionals who offer services through The Art of Connect.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

This Professional Provider Agreement ("Agreement") is between **The Art of Connect, LLC** ("The Art of Connect," "we," "us") and the counselor, coach, mentor or other professional ("Provider," "you") who applies to offer services to members through theartofconnect.com and its related experiences: **The Professional Society — In Business**, **The Art of Becoming — In Life** and **The Personal Society — In Love**.

This Agreement works alongside our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service), [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy) and [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards). If this Agreement conflicts with those documents on a matter specific to Providers, this Agreement controls.

## 1. Who this Agreement covers

This Agreement applies to every professional who applies for, or holds, a Provider account, including:

- **Licensed mental-health professionals**, such as licensed professional counselors, licensed marriage and family therapists, licensed clinical social workers, psychologists and similar licensed clinicians.
- **Coaches**, including life, relationship, executive, career and wellness coaches, whether or not they hold a private certification.
- **Mentors**, including experienced business leaders and professionals who offer guidance through The Professional Society.
- **Other non-clinical professionals** offering educational, personal-development or advisory services that we approve.

The category you apply under determines which verification steps apply to you and how your profile is described to members.

## 2. Licensed services versus coaching, mentorship and personal development

The Art of Connect draws a clear line between these kinds of services, and you must respect it in everything you say and do on the platform:

- **Licensed mental-health services** are the assessment, diagnosis or treatment of mental-health conditions by a professional who holds a current license to provide those services in the client's jurisdiction.
- **Coaching** helps a person set and pursue goals. **Coaching is not therapy.** Coaches must not diagnose, treat or claim to treat any mental-health condition, and must refer members to licensed professionals when a need falls outside coaching.
- **Mentorship** shares professional experience and perspective. It is not legal, financial, tax, investment or clinical advice unless the mentor is separately licensed and clearly states that they are providing such advice in that capacity.
- **Educational content and personal development**, including the guided reflection, journals and assessments in **The Art of Becoming — In Life**, are self-reflection tools. They are not clinical services.

You must describe your services accurately within the category for which you were approved.

## 3. Not an emergency service; no clinical treatment by the platform

The Art of Connect is **not an emergency service** and does not monitor messages, journals or appointments in real time. The Art of Connect itself does **not provide clinical treatment**. If a member indicates a risk of harm to themselves or others, you must follow your own professional, ethical and legal obligations, which may include directing the member to call **911** (or local emergency services) or the **988 Suicide & Crisis Lifeline** (call or text 988 in the United States).

## 4. Independent contractor relationship

- You are an **independent professional**. You are not an employee, agent, partner or joint venturer of The Art of Connect.
- You control how you deliver your services, including your methods, schedule (subject to the platform's booking tools) and professional judgment.
- You are solely responsible for your own taxes, business licenses, registrations, insurance, record-keeping and compliance with laws and professional rules that apply to you.
- You may not represent that The Art of Connect employs, supervises, endorses or guarantees your services. A "verified" badge means only that we completed the checks described in Section 5 at the time they were performed.

## 5. Credential and identity verification

Before your profile is published, our staff complete a verification checklist. **Approval is refused until every applicable item is complete.** The checklist includes:

1. **Identity** — confirmation that you are who you say you are, which may use a third-party identity verification provider. We do not store copies of government ID documents ourselves.
2. **License lookup** — for licensed professionals, verification of your license number, type, status and expiration with the issuing state board or official registry.
3. **Disciplinary check** — review of available public records of disciplinary action, restrictions or sanctions.
4. **Insurance** — confirmation of professional liability insurance where required under Section 7.
5. **References** — confirmation of professional references where we request them.

You agree that the information you provide is true, complete and current, and you authorize us to verify it with the relevant boards, registries and references. Verification is a point-in-time check. It is not a guarantee of your skill, conduct or the outcome of any service.

## 6. License expiration and reverification

- You must keep every license and credential you rely on **current and in good standing** for as long as you hold a Provider account.
- You must notify us at **info@theartofconnect.com** within **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: notification deadline, e.g. 5 business days]** of any expiration, lapse, suspension, restriction, probation, disciplinary action, complaint resulting in formal action, or change in insurance coverage.
- We will reverify credentials periodically, every **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: reverification interval]**, and before or at each license expiration date we have on record.
- If a license or required credential expires or is restricted, we may hide your profile, pause bookings or suspend your account until it is resolved.

## 7. Professional liability insurance

Where appropriate to your profession and services, and always for licensed mental-health professionals, you must maintain professional liability (malpractice or errors and omissions) insurance with minimum coverage of **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: minimum coverage amounts per claim and aggregate, and which provider categories must carry it]**. You must provide proof of coverage on request and keep it in force while you hold a Provider account.

## 8. Scope of practice and jurisdiction

- You may provide services **only within the scope of your license, training and approved category**.
- **Licensed providers may serve only clients located in states or jurisdictions where they are licensed** or otherwise legally authorized to practice, determined by the client's location at the time of the session.
- Rules for remote and telehealth services differ by state and profession, including interstate compacts, informed-consent requirements and platform security requirements. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: telehealth and interstate practice requirements by profession and state.]** You are responsible for knowing and following the rules that apply to you.
- Coaches and mentors must not provide services that require a license they do not hold.

## 9. Fees and platform membership charges

There are two separate kinds of charges:

- **Your professional fees.** You set the fees for your own services, subject to the platform's booking and payment tools and any policies we publish. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether session fees are collected through the platform, and any platform service fee or commission on session fees.]**
- **Platform membership charges.** Providers subscribe to a professional membership, currently the **Standard Provider**, **Professional Provider** or **Premium Provider** membership. The current price, billing interval and any onboarding fee are shown at checkout before you subscribe. Memberships renew automatically until cancelled, as described in our [Subscription and Automatic Renewal Policy](/legal/subscription-auto-renewal) and [Cancellation and Refund Policy](/legal/refund-policy).

We will give you advance notice of any change to your membership price, as described in those policies.

## 10. Appointments, cancellations and disputes

- You must keep the availability you publish accurate and honor appointments you accept.
- Cancellation and no-show terms must be clearly disclosed to members before booking. The platform's standard cancellation window is **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: platform cancellation window and no-show policy]**.
- If a member disputes a session, you agree to cooperate in good faith with our review. We may share relevant booking information with you and the member to resolve it. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: dispute resolution process and who decides refunds for session fees.]**

## 11. Confidentiality and professional obligations

- You must protect members' personal information and keep confidential what members share with you, consistent with your professional, ethical and legal obligations.
- **You are responsible for your own professional records.** The Art of Connect does not currently offer clinical record-keeping, and you should not use platform messaging or notes as your clinical record.
- The Art of Connect is **not represented as HIPAA compliant** and has not entered into Business Associate Agreements with Providers. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: HIPAA applicability and Business Associate Agreements before any clinical services are enabled on the platform.]**
- You may not access, request or use a member's private journal entries, assessments or communications with others unless the member chooses to share them with you directly.
- You may use member information only to provide the services the member requested, and not for your own marketing lists, resale or any other purpose.

## 12. Honest representation; no guarantees

You must not:

- misrepresent your identity, licenses, credentials, education, experience, affiliations or reviews;
- use titles such as "therapist," "counselor," "psychologist" or "licensed" unless you are legally entitled to use them in the member's jurisdiction;
- **guarantee outcomes**, including relationship success, marriage, reconciliation, business results, income or recovery from any condition;
- create fake reviews or ask members for reviews in exchange for discounts or other benefits.

## 13. Off-platform solicitation

You may not use the platform to solicit members to move bookings or payments off the platform in order to avoid platform policies or fees, except as our published policies allow. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether, and when, Providers may continue client relationships or take payments outside the platform.]** You must never solicit loans, investments, gifts or other financial benefits from members.

## 14. Professional conduct and Community Standards

You must follow our [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards) and the ethical code of your profession. Dating, romantic or sexual relationships with members who are your clients are prohibited. Harassment, discrimination and unwanted contact of any kind are prohibited.

## 15. Misconduct reporting, suspension and removal

- Members and staff may report concerns about a Provider through the reporting tools or at **info@theartofconnect.com**.
- We may investigate, request information from you, temporarily hide your profile or pause bookings while a report is reviewed.
- We may suspend or remove your Provider account for violations of this Agreement, loss of a required license or insurance, credible reports of misconduct, or conduct that puts members at risk.
- Where required by law or where appropriate, we may report serious misconduct to the relevant licensing board or authorities.
- **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: appeal process for Provider removals.]**

## 16. Data protection

- We process your personal information as described in our [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy), including to verify credentials, operate your account and process payments.
- You must keep your login secure, use two-step verification when offered or required, and notify us immediately of any suspected unauthorized access.
- If you learn of any unauthorized disclosure of member information connected with the platform, you must notify us promptly at info@theartofconnect.com.

## 17. Intellectual property

You keep ownership of your own content, such as your profile text and materials you create. You grant us a limited license to display that content to operate and promote the platform. You may not use The Art of Connect's names or logos, including The Professional Society, The Art of Becoming and The Personal Society, except as we permit in writing. See our [Intellectual Property and Copyright Policy](/legal/intellectual-property).

## 18. Indemnity and limitation of liability

**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: indemnity and limitation-of-liability terms, insurance interplay, and enforceability by state.]** In draft form: you agree to defend and indemnify The Art of Connect against claims arising from your services, your breach of this Agreement or your violation of law or professional rules. To the extent permitted by law, The Art of Connect is not liable for the services you provide to members.

## 19. Term and termination

You may close your Provider account at any time by cancelling your membership and notifying us. We may suspend or terminate this Agreement as described in Section 15 or if we discontinue the professional program. Sections that by their nature should survive termination, including confidentiality, indemnity and limitation of liability, will survive.

## 20. Changes to this Agreement

We may update this Agreement. We will notify you of material changes in advance and may ask you to accept the updated version before continuing to offer services. The version you accepted, and the date and time you accepted it, are recorded with your account.

## 21. Contact

The Art of Connect, LLC · **info@theartofconnect.com**$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('safety-policy', 'Member Safety and Reporting Policy', 'safety', 'How we help keep members safe, how to report and block, and how we investigate and respond.', 'safety', '{}', '{}', 130);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('safety-policy', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Member Safety and Reporting Policy', 'How we help keep members safe, how to report and block, and how we investigate and respond.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

Your safety and dignity matter to us. This policy explains the protections The Art of Connect, LLC ("The Art of Connect," "we," "us") provides across The Professional Society (In Business), The Art of Becoming (In Life) and The Personal Society (In Love), what we ask of you, and what happens when you report a concern. It should be read with our [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards) and [Identity and Age Verification Policy](/legal/identity-verification).

## 1. An honest word about safety
We work hard to create a trusted environment for adults aged 40 and older, but no online service can remove every risk. **The Art of Connect cannot guarantee the identity, intentions, honesty or conduct of any member, couple or professional provider**, whether online or in person. Please use the same judgment you would use when meeting anyone new, and use the tools described below.

## 2. The protections we provide
- **Age eligibility.** Consumer membership is limited to adults aged 40 and older. You confirm your date of birth at registration, and your date of birth is stored privately and never shown on your profile.
- **Identity and age verification.** We may require or offer verification through our third-party provider, Stripe Identity. See section 5 for what verification does and does not mean.
- **Private by design.** Your journals, reflections and assessment answers are private to you. Contact details are not displayed on profiles.
- **Blocking and reporting** tools in every experience.
- **Automated and manual review** of signals such as repeated reports, suspicious sign-up patterns, payment fraud and identity mismatches, which may lead to restrictions while we review an account.
- **Professional credential review** for licensed providers before they are listed (see the [Professional Provider Agreement](/legal/professional-agreement)).
- **Account security** including strong passwords, secure password recovery and two-step verification for our staff.

**[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether criminal background checks or sex-offender registry screening are offered or required for any membership. If not offered, attorney to confirm any required state disclosure that background checks are not performed.]**

## 3. Warning signs of romance scams and financial fraud
Be cautious if someone:
- asks for money, gift cards, cryptocurrency, wire transfers, loans or help paying for travel, medical bills, customs fees or legal costs;
- introduces an investment, trading platform, cryptocurrency or "guaranteed" business opportunity;
- professes strong feelings very quickly, or pressures you to move the conversation off the platform;
- repeatedly avoids video calls or meeting in person, or gives inconsistent details about their life;
- claims to be working overseas, in the military, on an oil rig or in another situation that prevents meeting;
- asks for personal financial details, account numbers, passwords or verification codes.

**Never send money or share financial information with someone you have met through The Art of Connect.** Our team will never ask for your password or a verification code. If you suspect a scam, stop contact and report the person immediately. You may also report fraud to the FTC at reportfraud.ftc.gov and the FBI's Internet Crime Complaint Center at ic3.gov.

## 4. Meeting in person safely
When you decide to meet someone from The Personal Society or The Professional Society:
1. **Video call first** to confirm the person matches their profile.
2. **Meet in a public place** with other people around, such as a café, restaurant or hotel lobby. Avoid private homes for early meetings.
3. **Tell a friend or family member** where you are going, who you are meeting and when you expect to be home. Consider sharing your location with them.
4. **Arrange your own transportation** to and from the meeting, and do not accept a ride from someone you have just met.
5. **Keep personal details private** — your home address, workplace details and financial information — until you have built genuine trust.
6. **Stay in control** of your drinks and belongings, and limit alcohol.
7. **Trust your instincts.** You may leave at any time, for any reason.
8. **Report** any behavior that concerns you, even if nothing happened.

## 5. Identity and age verification — what it means and its limits
Verification through Stripe Identity compares an identity document with a live image of the person at a single point in time. A "verified" badge means only that **a document appeared to match the person completing the check when the check was performed.** It is **not** a criminal background check, does not confirm someone's character, marital status, finances or intentions, and does not guarantee that the account has not since been shared or compromised. We do not store copies of government identification documents ourselves; see our [Identity and Age Verification Policy](/legal/identity-verification).

## 6. Compatibility assessments are guidance, not guarantees
Assessments and compatibility insights are designed to support reflection and conversation. They are not psychological diagnoses or predictions, and they cannot guarantee romantic compatibility, a successful relationship or a successful business relationship. See our [Dating and Matchmaking Disclaimer](/legal/matchmaking-disclaimer).

## 7. How to block
You may block any member or provider from the member area at any time. Blocking:
- takes effect **immediately**;
- is **private** — the other person is not notified;
- prevents them from viewing your profile, appearing in your introductions or contacting you through the platform.

You can review and remove blocks in your safety settings.

## 8. How to report
Report a profile, message, appointment, review or behavior using the report option in the member area, or email **info@theartofconnect.com**. Helpful details include what happened, when, and any screenshots — but you do not need evidence or certainty to report a concern.
- Reports are **confidential.** We do not tell the reported person who reported them unless required by law.
- You may report conduct that happened off the platform, including at an in-person meeting, if it involves another member.
- Professional misconduct by a provider can be reported the same way; we may also refer it to the relevant licensing board.

## 9. How we respond
1. **Triage.** We prioritize reports involving threats, violence, minors, sexual misconduct, fraud and self-harm.
2. **Protective steps.** Where there is a credible risk, we may immediately restrict or suspend the reported account while we investigate.
3. **Review.** Trained team members review the report, relevant account activity and any history of prior reports. Staff access is limited to what is needed for the investigation and is recorded in our audit logs. Private journals and assessment answers are not accessed for investigations.
4. **Decision.** Outcomes may include no action, a warning, removal of content, feature limits, suspension or permanent closure, as described in our Community Standards.
5. **Follow-up.** We will let you know we have received your report. For privacy reasons we may not be able to share the specific action taken against another account.

**[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: target response times for urgent and non-urgent reports.]**

## 10. Law enforcement
We may share information with law enforcement where we believe in good faith that it is necessary to prevent imminent harm, to respond to valid legal process, or as otherwise permitted or required by law, as described in our [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy). If you have been the victim of a crime, we encourage you to contact local law enforcement. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: law-enforcement request procedures and preservation obligations.]**

## 11. Appeals
If action is taken on your account, you may request a review as described in section 11 of our [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards). **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: appeal timeframe.]**

## 12. Emergencies and crisis support
The Art of Connect is **not an emergency service** and does not monitor conversations in real time. If you or someone else is in immediate danger, call **911**. For emotional crisis or thoughts of suicide, call or text **988** (Suicide & Crisis Lifeline). For domestic violence support, contact the National Domestic Violence Hotline at 1-800-799-7233.

## 13. State-specific notices
**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: state dating-service laws (e.g. safety awareness notices, background-check disclosures in states such as New York, New Jersey, Illinois, Texas, Florida) and any required wording, placement or acknowledgment.]**

## 14. Contact
Safety questions and reports: **info@theartofconnect.com**.$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('identity-verification', 'Identity and Age Verification Policy', 'privacy', 'How The Art of Connect confirms that members are 40 or older and who they say they are, what information is used, and the limits of verification.', 'identity_verification', '{}', '{}', 140);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('identity-verification', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Identity and Age Verification Policy', 'How The Art of Connect confirms that members are 40 or older and who they say they are, what information is used, and the limits of verification.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

The Art of Connect is a community exclusively for adults aged **40 and older**. This policy explains how **The Art of Connect, LLC** ("we," "us") confirms age eligibility and identity, what information is involved, and what verification can and cannot tell you.

## 1. Why we verify
Verification helps keep our community authentic and safe. It reduces fake profiles, impersonation and romance scams, and it supports our age requirement.

## 2. Age eligibility at registration
When you register, you provide your date of birth. Our system will not create a consumer membership account for anyone younger than the minimum age, which is currently 40. The minimum age is set by the owner and can be raised.

Your date of birth is stored in a private record that only you can read. Our staff, including the owner, see only whether your account meets the age requirement. Your date of birth is never shown on your profile and is never included in emails.

## 3. Identity verification
Some features or memberships may require identity verification, for example before introductions in In Love or before a professional is listed. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: which memberships or features require identity verification, and whether it is required at registration]**

Identity verification is performed by **Stripe Identity**, a third-party provider. During verification you may be asked to:
- photograph a government-issued photo ID; and
- take a live selfie so the provider can compare it with your ID photo.

**The Art of Connect does not receive or store images of your ID or your selfie.** Stripe processes them under its own privacy terms. We receive only:
- the verification outcome (for example, verified, requires more information, or not verified);
- the date of the check; and
- a reference to the verification session so we can resolve problems.

Where the provider confirms a date of birth, we use it only to confirm age eligibility.

**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: biometric laws (Illinois BIPA, Texas, Washington) for Stripe Identity selfie checks — notice, written consent and retention schedule requirements]**

## 4. Consent
Before verification begins, we will tell you what the provider will collect and ask you to agree. Verification consent is separate from other agreements and from marketing consent. If you do not consent, you can still use features that do not require verification.

## 5. Cost
**[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether verification is included in membership or charged separately]** Identity verification charges are not active and will not be activated without the owner's authorization.

## 6. Professionals
Counselors, coaches and mentors go through a separate credential review described in the [Professional Provider Agreement](/legal/professional-agreement), which may include license verification with the relevant licensing board, disciplinary checks, insurance confirmation and references.

## 7. Limits of verification
Verification confirms that a person matched an identity document at a point in time. **It does not:**
- guarantee that a person is honest, safe, single, financially secure, or who they claim to be in every respect;
- reveal criminal history (we do not currently conduct criminal background checks **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED / ATTORNEY REVIEW]**);
- guarantee compatibility or the outcome of any relationship or business connection.

Always follow our [Member Safety and Reporting Policy](/legal/safety-policy), especially before meeting someone in person or sending money.

## 8. Failed or unresolved verification
If verification fails or cannot be completed, features that require it remain unavailable. You may try again. If we believe an account is using false identity information, we may suspend or close it under our [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards). You may appeal by writing to info@theartofconnect.com.

## 9. Misrepresentation
Lying about your age or identity, using another person's documents, or helping someone bypass verification violates our Terms and will result in account removal.

## 10. Couples
Each partner in a Couples Membership has a separate account and, where verification is required, completes verification individually. One partner's verification result is never shown to the other unless that partner chooses to share it.

## 11. Verification badges
**[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether verified members display a badge to others]** If badges are used, they will show only that verification was completed — never the document type, document details or date of birth — and members will be reminded of the limits described in section 7.

## 12. Accessibility and alternatives
If you cannot complete automated verification because of a disability, lack of a qualifying ID, or a technical problem, contact info@theartofconnect.com. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED / ATTORNEY REVIEW: alternative verification method and accessibility accommodations]**

## 13. Retention
We keep the verification outcome for **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED]**. Stripe's retention of verification images and data is governed by Stripe's terms. See our [Data Retention and Account Deletion Policy](/legal/data-retention).

## 14. Reporting suspected false identity
If you believe a member is using a false identity, misrepresenting their age, or impersonating someone, use the Report option on their profile or email info@theartofconnect.com. Do not confront the person or send them money. Our safety team reviews every report and may require the member to verify again, restrict their account during review, or remove them.

## 15. Changes
We will update this policy before changing verification providers or methods, and will ask for renewed consent where required.

## 16. Contact
**info@theartofconnect.com**$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('cookie-policy', 'Cookie and Tracking Policy', 'privacy', 'The cookies and similar technologies The Art of Connect uses, why we use them, and how you can control them.', 'cookies', '{}', '{}', 150);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('cookie-policy', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Cookie and Tracking Policy', 'The cookies and similar technologies The Art of Connect uses, why we use them, and how you can control them.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

This Cookie and Tracking Policy explains how **The Art of Connect, LLC** ("we," "us") uses cookies and similar technologies on theartofconnect.com and within our member, professional and owner portals. It supplements our [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy).

## 1. What cookies are
Cookies are small text files a website stores in your browser. Similar technologies include local storage and scripts that help a page work. "First-party" cookies are set by our own website; "third-party" cookies are set by another company.

## 2. Our approach
We keep tracking to a minimum. Today we use:
- **Essential cookies** that make sign-in and security work; and
- **First-party attribution cookies** that remember which campaign or member referral brought you to us.

We do **not** currently use third-party advertising cookies, advertising pixels, cross-site tracking, or social-media tracking scripts. We do not sell information collected through cookies.

## 3. Cookies we use

### 3.1 Essential (strictly necessary)
| Purpose | Set by | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| Sign-in session | The Art of Connect (via Supabase Auth) | Keeps you securely signed in and refreshes your session. Without it you cannot use your account. |
| Security checks | The Art of Connect | Supports protections such as two-factor authentication for staff and safe redirects after sign-in. |

These cookies are required for the service to function and cannot be switched off in our settings. You can block them in your browser, but sign-in will not work.

### 3.2 Attribution (first-party)
| Purpose | What it stores | Duration |
|---|---|---|
| Campaign source | The marketing campaign details in the link you followed (such as source and campaign name) | **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: confirm attribution cookie lifetime currently set in the website code]** |
| Referral code | A member's referral code from the link you followed, so the referral can be credited | Same as above |

These cookies are set only by our own website, are marked secure and HTTP-only, and are not shared with advertising networks.

**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: whether attribution cookies require opt-in or notice-only treatment under applicable state laws and, if non-US visitors are accepted, ePrivacy rules]**

### 3.3 Bot protection
When you use sign-in, registration, password recovery, the notify-me list or professional forms, **Cloudflare Turnstile** runs a privacy-focused check to tell people from automated bots. Cloudflare may process technical information about your browser and connection to perform this check. Cloudflare's own privacy terms apply to that processing.

### 3.4 Payments and identity verification
When you pay for a membership you are taken to **Stripe** Checkout, and if identity verification is required you use **Stripe Identity**. Stripe sets its own cookies on its pages for fraud prevention and security. Stripe's privacy terms apply to those pages.

### 3.5 Analytics
We do not currently use third-party website analytics. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether to add an analytics provider; if so, which provider, what is collected, and whether consent is requested first]** This policy will be updated, and consent requested where required, before any analytics are enabled.

## 4. Browser storage
Some pages store small preferences in your browser (for example, a selection you made in the membership builder so it is still there if you return). This information stays on your device.

## 5. Email
Our transactional emails are sent through **Resend**. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether open or click tracking is enabled in email]** We do not use email tracking to build advertising profiles.

## 6. Your choices
- **Browser controls:** most browsers let you view, block and delete cookies. Blocking essential cookies will prevent sign-in.
- **Global Privacy Control:** **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED / ATTORNEY REVIEW: how the site will honor Global Privacy Control and other opt-out preference signals]**
- **Marketing:** marketing email consent is separate from cookies and can be withdrawn at any time.

## 7. What we never do with cookies
- We do not use cookies to read or infer the contents of your private journals, assessments, romantic preferences or messages.
- We do not use cookies to build advertising profiles or to show you advertising on other websites.
- We do not allow advertising networks or data brokers to place cookies through our website.
- We do not sell or share information collected through cookies for cross-context behavioral advertising.

## 8. Member, professional and Owner Portal areas
Private areas of the website (your member dashboard, the professional portal and the Owner Portal) use only essential cookies. These pages are marked so that browsers and search engines do not store or index them, and they are never cached by our hosting provider. Staff who sign in to the Owner Portal must also complete two-factor authentication; the security state of that session is held in an essential cookie.

## 9. Sharing a device
If you share a computer or tablet with someone else, sign out when you finish so that your session cookie is removed. You can also ask us to sign your account out of every device by writing to info@theartofconnect.com.

## 10. Do Not Track and preference signals
Browsers offer "Do Not Track" and similar settings. Because we do not use third-party tracking, these settings do not change how our website behaves today. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: obligations to recognize opt-out preference signals in states that require it]**

## 11. Changes
If we add new cookies or tracking technologies, we will update this policy, change its version and effective date, and, where required, ask for your consent before using them.

## 12. Contact
Questions about cookies: **info@theartofconnect.com**$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('data-retention', 'Data Retention and Account Deletion Policy', 'privacy', 'How long The Art of Connect keeps different kinds of information and how members can close their accounts and request deletion.', 'data_retention', '{}', '{}', 160);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('data-retention', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Data Retention and Account Deletion Policy', 'How long The Art of Connect keeps different kinds of information and how members can close their accounts and request deletion.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

This policy explains how **The Art of Connect, LLC** ("we," "us") decides how long to keep information and how you can close your account and request deletion. It supplements our [Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy).

## 1. Principles
1. We keep personal information only as long as it is needed to provide the service, meet legal and financial obligations, keep the community safe, and resolve disputes.
2. Sensitive information — private journals, assessments, romantic preferences, private communications and identity verification results — receives the shortest practical retention.
3. Where we must keep a record (for example, for tax or payment purposes), we keep only what the obligation requires.
4. We do not keep ID document images at all; identity checks are handled by Stripe Identity.

## 2. Retention by category
The periods below are **not yet decided** and must be set by the owner with legal advice. Until they are approved, this table describes what each category contains and what drives its retention.

| Category | What it includes | Retention |
|---|---|---|
| Account profile | Name, email, display name, account status | **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: retention period for closed accounts]** |
| Date of birth | Stored privately, visible only to you | Deleted with your account, unless **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: whether proof of age eligibility must be retained]** |
| Private journals and assessments | In Life and In Love content | Deleted when you delete them or close your account. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: grace period, if any, before permanent deletion]** |
| Private messages | Conversations with members or professionals | **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: retention after account closure, considering the other participant's copy and safety investigations]** |
| Safety reports and enforcement records | Reports, blocks, suspensions, appeals | **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED / ATTORNEY REVIEW: retention needed to prevent banned users from returning]** |
| Identity verification outcome | Verified / not verified, date, provider reference | **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED]** (images are never held by us) |
| Payment and subscription records | Amounts, dates, status, refunds (no card numbers) | **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: tax and accounting retention requirements]** |
| Consent and agreement acceptance records | Which document version you accepted and when | Kept as evidence of the agreement. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: retention period for contract evidence]** |
| Security logs | Sign-in events with hashed IP address | **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: security log retention period]** |
| Financial and administrative audit trail | Changes to prices, refunds, permissions and launch settings | Kept permanently and cannot be altered, as a control record. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: confirm appropriate retention]** |
| Professional credential records | Application, license details, verification checklist | **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: retention for credentialing and complaint handling]** |
| Notify-me list | Email and membership interests | Until you ask us to remove you or **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED]** |
| Backups | Encrypted database backups held by our hosting provider | Deleted information may remain in backups until they expire. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: backup plan and retention]** |

## 3. Closing your account
You can ask to close your account at any time by writing to **info@theartofconnect.com** from the email address on your account. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: in-account self-service deletion]**

Before closing an account with an active paid membership, please cancel your membership (see the [Cancellation and Refund Policy](/legal/refund-policy)). Closing an account does not by itself issue a refund.

When your account is closed:
1. You are signed out of all devices.
2. Your profile is removed from matching, directories and introductions.
3. Your private journals, assessments and preferences are deleted, subject to any grace period above.
4. Records we must keep (for example, payment records and agreement acceptances) are retained only for the required period and then deleted or de-identified.

## 4. Couples
Each partner has a separate account. Closing your account does not close your partner's account. Content you added to a shared relationship space may remain visible to your partner. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED / ATTORNEY REVIEW: what happens to shared-space content when one partner leaves]**

## 5. Professionals
Professionals who close their accounts are removed from the directory. Records about appointments and client relationships may be subject to professional record-keeping obligations that belong to the professional, not to The Art of Connect. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW]**

## 6. Legal holds
We may keep information longer when required by law, a court order, an ongoing investigation, or to establish or defend legal claims.

## 7. De-identified information
We may keep aggregated or de-identified information that can no longer reasonably identify you, for example total membership counts.

## 8. Requests and timelines
We will confirm receipt of deletion requests and respond within the period required by applicable law. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: state response timelines and verification standards]**

## 9. Deleting specific content without closing your account
You do not have to close your account to remove information. You can:
- delete individual journal entries and assessment results from your private space;
- remove profile details you no longer want shown;
- withdraw optional consents, such as marketing email or partner sharing; and
- ask us to remove you from the notify-me list.

Deleted content is removed from your account immediately and from our active systems as described above, subject to backups.

## 10. Information others hold
Some information about you may be held by others: a match may remember a conversation, a professional may keep their own client records under their professional obligations, and Stripe keeps payment and verification records under its own terms. Our deletion process covers information held by The Art of Connect and asks our service providers to delete information they hold on our behalf.

## 11. Changes
We will update this policy as retention decisions are approved and will notify members of material changes.

## 12. Contact
**info@theartofconnect.com**$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('intellectual-property', 'Intellectual Property and Copyright Policy', 'company', 'Who owns the brands, content and materials on The Art of Connect, and how to report copyright infringement.', 'intellectual_property', '{}', '{}', 170);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('intellectual-property', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Intellectual Property and Copyright Policy', 'Who owns the brands, content and materials on The Art of Connect, and how to report copyright infringement.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

This policy explains how intellectual property works on the services of **The Art of Connect, LLC** ("The Art of Connect," "we," "us"), and how to report content you believe infringes your copyright. It is part of our [Terms of Service](/legal/terms-of-service).

## 1. What The Art of Connect owns

The Art of Connect owns, or is licensed to use, the platform and its content, including:

- the names, logos, monograms, taglines and visual identity of **The Art of Connect**, **The Professional Society**, **The Art of Becoming** and **The Personal Society**, including "In Business. In Life. In Love.";
- the website, apps, software, design, layouts and graphics;
- written, audio and video content we create, including guided reflections, prompts, assessments, educational materials, emails and marketing;
- the structure and wording of our compatibility, readiness and emotional-intelligence assessments.

**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: trademark registration status and filing strategy for each brand name and logo.]** Until registrations are confirmed, these marks are used as common-law trademarks and are not described as registered.

## 2. What you may do with our content

As a member, you receive a limited, personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable and revocable license to use our content for your own personal use while your membership is active. You may not:

- copy, sell, republish, distribute or create derivative works from our content;
- use our names, logos or brand elements in any way that suggests endorsement or affiliation without our written permission;
- scrape, harvest or bulk-download content or member information;
- reverse-engineer or copy the platform, its software or its assessments.

## 3. What you own

You keep ownership of the content you create, such as your profile text, photos, messages and journal entries ("Your Content").

You grant The Art of Connect a limited, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to host, store, display and process Your Content **only as needed to operate, secure and provide the services to you**. For example, we display your profile to the members you choose to be visible to.

This license:

- does **not** allow us to sell Your Content;
- does **not** allow us to use your private journal entries, assessment answers or private communications for advertising or to train artificial-intelligence models;
- ends when you delete Your Content or your account, except for copies we must keep for legal, security or backup reasons as described in our [Data Retention and Account Deletion Policy](/legal/data-retention).

**Private journal entries stay private.** They are visible only to you unless you choose to share them.

You must have the rights to anything you upload. Do not upload photos of other people, or content created by others, without permission.

## 4. Professional providers' content

Counselors, coaches and mentors keep ownership of the materials they create and grant us a limited license to display their profiles and approved materials, as described in the [Professional Provider Agreement](/legal/professional-agreement).

## 5. Feedback

If you send us ideas or suggestions, we may use them to improve the services without any obligation to you. We will not publish your name with your feedback without permission.

## 6. Reporting copyright infringement

If you believe content on the platform infringes your copyright, send a written notice to our designated copyright agent containing:

1. your physical or electronic signature;
2. identification of the copyrighted work you believe was infringed;
3. identification of the infringing material and where it appears on the platform, with enough detail for us to find it;
4. your name, address, telephone number and email address;
5. a statement that you have a good-faith belief that the use is not authorized by the copyright owner, its agent or the law;
6. a statement, under penalty of perjury, that the information in your notice is accurate and that you are the copyright owner or authorized to act on the owner's behalf.

**Designated copyright agent:** The Art of Connect, LLC, **info@theartofconnect.com**. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: designated copyright agent name and mailing address, and registration of the agent with the U.S. Copyright Office's DMCA Designated Agent Directory.]**

We may remove or disable access to the material and will notify the member who posted it.

## 7. Counter-notice

If your content was removed and you believe that was a mistake or misidentification, you may send a counter-notice to our copyright agent including:

1. your physical or electronic signature;
2. identification of the removed material and where it appeared;
3. a statement, under penalty of perjury, that you have a good-faith belief the material was removed by mistake or misidentification;
4. your name, address and telephone number, and a statement that you consent to the jurisdiction of the federal court for your address (or, if outside the United States, any judicial district where The Art of Connect may be found) and will accept service of process from the person who filed the original notice.

If we receive a valid counter-notice, we may restore the material after the waiting period required by law unless the original complainant notifies us that they have filed a court action. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: DMCA safe-harbor requirements and process timing.]**

## 8. Repeat infringers

We may suspend or close the accounts of members who repeatedly infringe others' intellectual property.

## 9. Trademark and other concerns

To report misuse of a trademark, impersonation or other intellectual-property concerns, email **info@theartofconnect.com** with details. Impersonation of members is also covered by our [Community Standards](/legal/community-standards).

## 10. Contact

The Art of Connect, LLC · **info@theartofconnect.com**$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('accessibility', 'Accessibility Statement', 'company', 'Our commitment to making The Art of Connect usable by everyone, and how to get help or request alternate formats.', 'accessibility', '{}', '{}', 180);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('accessibility', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Accessibility Statement', 'Our commitment to making The Art of Connect usable by everyone, and how to get help or request alternate formats.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

**The Art of Connect, LLC** ("The Art of Connect," "we," "us") wants every adult aged 40 and older to be able to use our website and services comfortably, including people who use assistive technology or have vision, hearing, motor or cognitive disabilities.

## 1. Our goal

We are working toward conformance with the **Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2, Level AA**, published by the World Wide Web Consortium.

We **do not currently claim** that the website or services conform to WCAG 2.2 AA. We have not yet completed a formal accessibility audit. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether and when to commission an independent third-party accessibility audit.]**

## 2. What we have built so far

Accessibility features already built into the website include:

- **Keyboard navigation.** Menus, forms, buttons and the membership builder can be used with a keyboard.
- **Visible focus states.** The element you are on is clearly outlined when you navigate by keyboard.
- **Reduced motion.** If your device is set to reduce motion, animations and moving effects are switched off.
- **Text alternatives.** Meaningful images have text descriptions, and decorative images are hidden from screen readers.
- **Responsive layouts.** Pages adapt to phones, tablets and computers and support browser zoom.
- **Readable design.** We choose text sizes, spacing and color contrast with legibility in mind, and we label form fields and error messages clearly.
- **Semantic structure.** Pages use headings, landmarks and labels so screen readers can navigate them.

## 3. Known limitations

Because we have not completed an audit, some areas may not yet meet our goal. These may include:

- color contrast on some decorative or brand-styled elements;
- complex interactive elements, such as the membership builder, with some screen reader and browser combinations;
- third-party features such as payment pages (Stripe), identity verification and bot-protection checks (Cloudflare Turnstile), whose accessibility is managed by those providers;
- older documents or images that may lack full text alternatives.

We will update this statement as we find and fix issues.

## 4. Security checks

To protect members, some forms use an automated bot check. It is designed to run without a puzzle for most people. If a check stops you from signing in, joining or contacting us, email us and we will help you directly.

## 5. Requesting help or an alternate format

If you have difficulty using any part of our website or services, or need a document such as a policy or agreement in another format (for example large print or plain text), contact us:

- **Email:** info@theartofconnect.com
- Include the page or feature, what you were trying to do, and the assistive technology you use, if any.

We aim to respond within **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: response time commitment, e.g. 2 business days]** and will work with you to provide the information or service in a way that works for you.

## 6. Ongoing work

We plan to:

- test new features for keyboard and screen reader use before release;
- review color contrast and text sizing across the site;
- include accessibility in our design and development checklists;
- review this statement at least once a year. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: review schedule and responsible person.]**

**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: applicable accessibility obligations, including the Americans with Disabilities Act and state laws, for an online membership service.]**

## 7. Feedback

We welcome feedback on accessibility. Email **info@theartofconnect.com**.

## 8. Contact

The Art of Connect, LLC · **info@theartofconnect.com**$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

insert into public.legal_documents (slug, title, category, summary, consent_key, required_at, brands, sort_order) values ('security-disclosure', 'Security and Responsible Vulnerability Disclosure Policy', 'privacy', 'How The Art of Connect protects the platform and how security researchers can report vulnerabilities responsibly.', 'security_disclosure', '{}', '{}', 190);
insert into public.legal_document_versions (document_slug, version_label, title, summary, body, change_summary) values ('security-disclosure', '2026-12-draft-1', 'Security and Responsible Vulnerability Disclosure Policy', 'How The Art of Connect protects the platform and how security researchers can report vulnerabilities responsibly.', $legal$*Draft pending owner approval and attorney review — not yet in effect.*

**The Art of Connect, LLC** ("we," "us") takes the security of our members' information seriously. This policy describes our security practices in general terms and explains how to report a potential vulnerability.

## 1. Our security practices
We describe these practices so members understand how their information is protected. They are not a guarantee, and no system is perfectly secure.
- **Separation of member data:** our database enforces row-level security so that members can read only their own private records. Private journals, assessments and confidential communications are not visible to staff, including the owner.
- **Encryption in transit:** the website and our service providers use HTTPS.
- **Staff access:** staff permissions are assigned by role, and every staff account must use two-factor authentication before accessing the Owner Portal.
- **Audit trails:** administrative and financial changes are recorded, including who made a change and when. Financial records cannot be altered after they are written.
- **Bot protection and rate limiting:** sign-in, registration, password recovery and public forms are protected by Cloudflare Turnstile and per-visitor rate limits.
- **Payments:** card details are handled by Stripe and never stored by us.
- **Identity documents:** handled by Stripe Identity and never stored by us.
- **Security logs:** record hashed IP addresses rather than raw addresses and never contain passwords or private content.
- **Automated checks:** code changes are checked for exposed secrets and known dependency vulnerabilities, and database permission tests run before release.

We do not claim any security certification (such as SOC 2 or ISO 27001). **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether to pursue a formal certification or third-party penetration test before launch]**

## 2. Reporting a vulnerability
If you believe you have found a security vulnerability in theartofconnect.com or our services, please email **info@theartofconnect.com** with the subject line "Security report." **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: dedicated security reporting address, e.g. security@theartofconnect.com]**

Please include:
- a description of the issue and where it occurs;
- steps to reproduce it;
- the potential impact; and
- how we can contact you.

Please do not include other people's personal information in your report.

## 3. What we ask of researchers
To protect our members, please:
1. Test only with accounts you own or have explicit permission to use.
2. Do not access, modify, download or delete other members' data. If you encounter it accidentally, stop, do not keep it, and tell us.
3. Do not read or attempt to read private journals, assessments or messages.
4. Do not perform denial-of-service attacks, spam, social engineering or physical attacks.
5. Do not use automated scanning that degrades the service for others.
6. Give us reasonable time to fix the issue before sharing it publicly. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: disclosure timeline, e.g. 90 days]**

## 4. Out of scope
- Third-party services we use (Supabase, Netlify, Stripe, Resend, Cloudflare) — report issues in their systems directly to them.
- Reports that only describe best-practice suggestions without a demonstrable security impact.
- Issues requiring physical access to a user's device.

## 5. Our commitments
When you report in good faith under this policy, we will:
- acknowledge your report within **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: response time]**;
- keep you informed as we investigate and fix the issue; and
- credit you publicly if you wish, once the issue is resolved.

## 6. Safe harbor
**[ATTORNEY REVIEW: good-faith safe harbor language — e.g. that we will not pursue legal action against researchers who comply with this policy — and its interaction with computer misuse laws]**

## 7. Rewards
We do not currently offer a bug bounty or payment for reports. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether to offer rewards]**

## 8. Security incidents affecting members
If a security incident affects your personal information, we will investigate promptly, take steps to contain it, and notify affected members and regulators as required by law. **[ATTORNEY REVIEW: state breach-notification timelines and content requirements]**

## 9. Protecting your own account
You play an important part in keeping your account secure:
- Use a unique password of at least 12 characters that you do not use on any other website.
- Never share your password or a sign-in link with anyone, including someone you met on the platform.
- We will never ask for your password by email, phone or message.
- Be cautious of messages that pressure you to act quickly, click unfamiliar links or move a conversation off the platform.
- Sign out on shared devices.

## 10. Scope
This policy covers theartofconnect.com, our member dashboard, the professional portal, the Owner Portal and our account and payment flows. **[OWNER DECISION REQUIRED: whether staging or preview environments are in scope]**

## 11. Reporting account security concerns
If you think your own account has been compromised, change your password immediately and email **info@theartofconnect.com**. Our team can sign your account out of every device.

## 12. Phishing and impersonation of The Art of Connect
Our emails come only from our verified theartofconnect.com domain and never ask for your password, payment card details or identity documents by reply. If you receive a message claiming to be from The Art of Connect that asks for these, do not respond; forward it to info@theartofconnect.com so we can investigate and warn other members.

## 13. Changes
We may update this policy as our security program grows. The version and effective date appear at the top.

## 14. Contact
**info@theartofconnect.com**$legal$, 'Initial company-specific draft for owner and attorney review.');

